Third-party inspiration
=======================

Clipbait reimplements techniques it learned from other open-source projects.
No source files were copied wholesale; where an approach was adapted, the
original project is credited here.

1. mutonby/openshorts — MIT
   https://github.com/mutonby/openshorts
   Adapted ideas: ASS subtitle structure with word-level karaoke timing, the
   `sendcmd` virtual-camera crop technique, split-screen and blur-bed layouts,
   and the shape of the FastAPI + SQLite job model. Clipbait's implementation
   was written independently and reorganised into the modules under
   `src/clipbait/{captions,reframe,render,live}`.

2. Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator — MIT
   https://github.com/Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator
   Adapted ideas: chunked highlight-scoring prompts and the score dimensions
   (hook, emotion, value, share) used in `src/clipbait/analyze`.

3. FujiwaraChoki/supoclip — design inspiration only
   https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip
   The project ships a non-commercial license. Clipbait used it strictly as a
   product/UX reference. No code, assets, prompts or copy were copied.

Full MIT license texts for items 1 and 2 are available in their repositories.


Runtime dependencies
====================

Clipbait links against these projects at runtime. They are installed from
PyPI or the system package manager, not vendored, and remain under their own
licenses:

  FastAPI, Starlette, Pydantic, Uvicorn, HTTPX, python-multipart,
  python-dotenv                                  — MIT / BSD (see packages)
  FFmpeg and FFprobe                             — LGPL/GPL depending on build
  yt-dlp                                         — Unlicense
  faster-whisper (optional)                      — MIT
  CTranslate2 (optional)                         — MIT
  OpenCV (optional)                              — Apache-2.0
  pytchat (optional)                             — MIT
  React, React DOM, React Router, Vite           — MIT

Clipbait does not ship fonts, music, stock footage or any third-party media.
Rendered clips contain only the source video you provide.


